{"id": "EUVD-2026-76277", "enisaUuid": "e392551b-4d2f-3417-bfcd-176f3aa70186", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ni3c: Fix unlocked dereference of dev->desc in i3c_device_get_supported_xfer_mode()\n\ni3c_device_get_supported_xfer_mode() uses dev->desc to obtain the\nmaster controller.  However, dev->desc must not be dereferenced unless\nbus->lock is held, and this function does not take that lock.\n\nThe function only needs access to the master controller associated with\nthe device's bus.  Use dev->bus instead, which is always valid for the\nlifetime of the device and does not require dereferencing dev->desc.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:38", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/251db58324ea4792c3f9f692ab09be148e051969", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8bed7f4fa710914b7f05fd59998316bfb4d43385"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5fmf-26vf-rg68", "CVE-2026-80954"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d938216-e073-307c-88e9-e47a6373d969", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19"}, {"id": "3ec7c1da-7b63-3487-8746-f4a9c1d30442", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "44740481-7fd6-3033-a6e4-74fc99893192", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "256a21743d911f94ce92fe28f793cd586f3860b2 <251db58324ea4792c3f9f692ab09be148e051969"}, {"id": "557a0ad1-0e42-386e-9759-d0cfc5b0f1a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "256a21743d911f94ce92fe28f793cd586f3860b2 <8bed7f4fa710914b7f05fd59998316bfb4d43385"}, {"id": "c7de3d26-c1a7-3a67-8907-b119fd7e1e52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "efdbb8fb-c7d6-3d